course: dictionary
lesson: 5205
title: January, a month with a capital letter
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: January is a proper noun. A proper noun is the name of one special person, place or thing, so it always starts with a capital letter: January, never january. It is the first month of the year, with 31 days, between December and February.
explain: Look at the words around it to understand it. «New Year's Day in January» tells you that January is the time when a new year begins. «January sales» tells you that shops have sales then. Notice that we say «in January», just as we say «in May» or «in June».
explain: Where you live changes what January feels like. In the UK, USA, Canada and Ireland, January is a winter month. In Australia and New Zealand, January is a summer month, so many children there have long summer holidays then. The name is the same everywhere, but the weather is not.
fact: January is the first month of the year and has 31 days.
fact: January always begins with a capital J, because it is a proper noun.
fact: January comes between December and February.
fact: The Earth is nearest the Sun in early January, even though it is winter in Britain then. So distance from the Sun cannot be what makes summer.
fact: «Bonne année!» (bo-na-NAY) means Happy New Year in French, and people say it all through January.
exercise: Which is written correctly as the name of the month? | *January | janUary | JANuary | january
exercise: «New Year's Day in January» is a phrase. What is January in this phrase? | A Scottish word for a wet day | A kind of summer holiday | The last month of the year | *The first month of the year
exercise: In which country is January a summer month? | *Australia | The United Kingdom | Canada | Ireland
test: The Earth is nearest the Sun in early January. What does this tell you? | Distance from the Sun is what makes summer | The Sun is cold in January | *Distance from the Sun cannot be what makes summer | January has no weather
test: Which month comes straight after January? | *February | December | April | March
exam: Why does January start with a capital letter? | *Because it is the name of one special month, a proper noun | Because it is a long word | Because it is a Scottish word | Because it is at the start of every sentence
